AuthoredPlacement.description:
An object an author stands on the surface (decision 085): its asset, by
ID of the surface's assets; its base's terrain-local point `[x, z]`,
where it stands on the ground; its turn about the vertical (degrees);
its scale (0.001 to 1000); how deep its base sinks, in meters at scale
1; how far it leans with the ground (0 upright, 1 along its normal);
and the pyramid level whose tiles hold it (0, the finest, by default;
coarser for objects seen from farther away).

bridge_fill.description:
Meters the road would fill above the ground beyond which it bridges
instead, as it does over rivers and lakes (decision 072), 0 to 1000;
0 never bridges.

SceneEnvironment.description:
A scene's look (decision 022). In a document, every omitted section takes
the engine's default state (sun shafts, reflections and refraction: off);
in a development control, omitted sections stay as they are.

max_resident_pages.description:
An optional budget of streamed pages (128 KiB each) kept resident;
beyond it the least recently used make room, and pinned pages always
stay. Omitted, only the device's limits bound them.
